  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_010 (multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is our best at 0.639 acc, and the multiprofile+weighted fusion combination is clearly superior to singleprofile (0.523) or concat fusion (0.619, at 3.4× the cost). The one untested axis within this exact architecture is the aggregation method: avgpool vs. transformer. Question: Does transformer-based aggregation (learning which profiles to emphasize) improve over simple average pooling while retaining the cheap weighted fusion? This is a single-variable extension of our best result, isolating the aggregation contribution. Rationale: With 6 experiments left, establishing whether transformer aggregation adds value is critical before investing in more expensive changes (larger image encoders, learned RNA encoders). If transformer helps, it becomes the new backbone for subsequent experiments; if not, we confirm avgpool suffices and redirect budget toward encoder upgrades. Expected cost: moderate, roughly 15–25 GPU hours (transformer attention over profiles adds cost over avgpool, but weighted fusion keeps it well below the 36+ hours seen with concat fusion)."
}

